WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:01.380
- Hey guys, I'm Curly.

00:00:01.380 --> 00:00:02.400
- I'm Jazzmyne.

00:00:02.400 --> 00:00:05.523
- And we're here for Queer
Prom 2018 in New York City.

00:00:05.580 --> 00:00:07.425
- Woo, and we're about to
go meet the court, let's go!

00:00:07.425 --> 00:00:08.714
(screaming)

00:00:08.714 --> 00:00:11.297
(upbeat music)

00:00:32.510 --> 00:00:33.343
- [Teo] Hello.

00:00:33.343 --> 00:00:34.650
- [Man] Hey Teo, how's it going?

00:00:34.650 --> 00:00:35.483
- [Teo] Hi, I'm great.

00:00:35.483 --> 00:00:36.730
- Well I wanted to introduce to my friend

00:00:36.730 --> 00:00:37.563
who had some news for you.

00:00:37.563 --> 00:00:38.396
- Hi!

00:00:38.770 --> 00:00:39.603
- Oh my God!

00:00:39.948 --> 00:00:40.781
- How are you?

00:00:40.954 --> 00:00:42.453
- Oh, my God, what, oh my God!

00:00:44.080 --> 00:00:46.130
- So we wanted to tell
you that you were selected

00:00:46.130 --> 00:00:47.885
and you are coming to New York to go to

00:00:47.885 --> 00:00:49.270
Buzzfeed's Queer Prom.
- You're serious?

00:00:49.270 --> 00:00:50.103
Oh my God.

00:00:50.103 --> 00:00:53.113
I feel like I came out to
myself when I was like, 10.

00:00:53.113 --> 00:00:54.441
(laughing)

00:00:54.630 --> 00:00:57.073
I was 10 years old like, okay,

00:00:57.510 --> 00:01:00.023
I wanna say this, why can't I say it?

00:01:00.180 --> 00:01:01.360
People are telling me I shouldn't

00:01:01.360 --> 00:01:02.310
be saying something like this.

00:01:02.310 --> 00:01:03.880
People are telling me I
shouldn't feel this way,

00:01:03.880 --> 00:01:05.150
so I didn't feel comfortable enough

00:01:05.150 --> 00:01:06.523
to share how I was feeling,

00:01:06.610 --> 00:01:09.163
and I guess it made me
a really angry person.

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:14.923
My father is something.

00:01:14.960 --> 00:01:17.060
He's very one of those people that's like,

00:01:18.800 --> 00:01:22.173
my kids are queer so I love queer people.

00:01:22.240 --> 00:01:23.863
And he says things like,

00:01:24.070 --> 00:01:26.210
oh, you wanna act like a man,

00:01:26.210 --> 00:01:27.723
then I'm gonna treat you like,

00:01:27.790 --> 00:01:28.950
I'ma talk to you like you're a man

00:01:28.950 --> 00:01:31.343
so you better man up, you better do this.

00:01:31.520 --> 00:01:34.100
And just because I identify as a trans guy

00:01:34.100 --> 00:01:37.596
doesn't mean I gotta be super
masculine 'cause I'm not.

00:01:37.596 --> 00:01:39.200
(laughing)

00:01:39.200 --> 00:01:43.223
Hi, so I'm in my room, it's late at night,

00:01:43.360 --> 00:01:45.070
and I just realized that there's

00:01:45.070 --> 00:01:46.790
only five days 'til Queer Prom.

00:01:46.790 --> 00:01:48.580
Living in Philly is many different things.

00:01:48.580 --> 00:01:51.803
It's really cool to be
around music creators,

00:01:51.930 --> 00:01:52.763
but at the same time,

00:01:52.763 --> 00:01:55.880
the people who I like to
surround myself with sometimes

00:01:56.280 --> 00:01:58.983
don't like me to be around
them, which can suck.

00:01:59.819 --> 00:02:01.986
(singing)

00:02:02.810 --> 00:02:05.010
I spend a lot of time in
the music scene in Philly,

00:02:05.010 --> 00:02:07.763
and it gets kinda scary,
it gets kinda upsetting,

00:02:07.810 --> 00:02:09.480
because a lot of the music business

00:02:09.480 --> 00:02:13.373
is homophobic and transphobic
and sexist and horrible.

00:02:15.310 --> 00:02:17.140
I had my sister at home and

00:02:17.140 --> 00:02:19.113
she was much more of a support system.

00:02:19.590 --> 00:02:22.830
She is probably the only person

00:02:23.470 --> 00:02:28.470
who I know that's always
supporting me like, my whole life.

00:02:29.640 --> 00:02:31.480
- Well, for me, I'm already queer.

00:02:31.480 --> 00:02:35.223
I came out as pansexual a long time ago,

00:02:35.280 --> 00:02:37.633
and everybody wasn't accepting of it.

00:02:37.970 --> 00:02:39.393
You came out twice, though.

00:02:39.820 --> 00:02:40.653
- Twice?

00:02:40.653 --> 00:02:41.860
- You came out twice, yeah.

00:02:41.860 --> 00:02:42.890
- I guess it happened.

00:02:42.890 --> 00:02:46.030
- You came out twice, but when
you came out as gay first,

00:02:46.030 --> 00:02:51.030
I was just like, okay, I know,
and then you're like, okay.

00:02:51.280 --> 00:02:53.120
And then the second
time, you were just like,

00:02:53.120 --> 00:02:57.113
I'm transgender, and I'm like,
alright, what's your name,

00:02:57.400 --> 00:03:00.150
what are your preferred
pronouns, alright, that's fine.

00:03:00.351 --> 00:03:03.101
(peaceful music)

00:03:07.170 --> 00:03:10.513
- I came out to my mom in
a 7-Eleven parking lot.

00:03:10.559 --> 00:03:12.809
(laughing)

00:03:14.310 --> 00:03:18.470
We were fighting, I think
over transgender rights,

00:03:18.470 --> 00:03:21.610
or something, and I was like,

00:03:21.610 --> 00:03:25.463
well Mom, I'm gay, and
then I ran out the car,

00:03:25.490 --> 00:03:27.660
went to 7-Eleven, went back to the car,

00:03:27.660 --> 00:03:30.060
and we stayed there crying
for at least an hour.

00:03:31.151 --> 00:03:34.010
All the 7-Eleven people
probably think we're crazy

00:03:34.010 --> 00:03:38.500
but, I'm so sorry, yeah, I love my mom.

00:03:38.500 --> 00:03:39.573
I wish she was here.

00:03:39.990 --> 00:03:41.640
So, we're getting ready to board

00:03:41.640 --> 00:03:44.540
our flight to New York
for Buzzfeed's Queer Prom.

00:03:44.670 --> 00:03:46.210
- [Eva's Mom] Abelena's my only niece,

00:03:46.210 --> 00:03:50.113
and she is the same age
as my daughter, Eva.

00:03:51.580 --> 00:03:55.393
- It means everything to be
able to be here for your mom,

00:03:55.440 --> 00:03:57.193
who loves you so much,

00:03:57.380 --> 00:04:00.843
and even though she's in
Nashville accepting an award,

00:04:01.240 --> 00:04:04.760
I am texting her like crazy
and sending her pictures

00:04:04.760 --> 00:04:07.460
and she's here with you every
minute, and we love you.

00:04:07.480 --> 00:04:10.493
- How has me being gay
affected our relationship?

00:04:13.499 --> 00:04:14.849
- I think we're closer now.

00:04:14.880 --> 00:04:19.880
I think you are able to open up more,

00:04:21.150 --> 00:04:26.150
and, which is a good
thing, it's a good thing.

00:04:27.338 --> 00:04:28.171
- Yeah.

00:04:28.171 --> 00:04:29.650
It's taken me a long time to be able

00:04:29.650 --> 00:04:31.820
to say I have a girlfriend out loud,

00:04:31.820 --> 00:04:33.950
'cause all the repercussions
that can happen

00:04:33.950 --> 00:04:36.890
in high school and the
cruelty of kids and I,

00:04:36.890 --> 00:04:39.150
honestly wanted to protect
her more than myself

00:04:39.150 --> 00:04:40.833
so I didn't want her to go through

00:04:40.833 --> 00:04:43.703
what I gone through in my past.

00:04:45.430 --> 00:04:49.330
And it was hard 'cause
I like her a little bit,

00:04:49.330 --> 00:04:52.870
you know, and it was hard
not being able to show

00:04:52.950 --> 00:04:54.730
our love and affection out in public,

00:04:54.730 --> 00:04:57.650
in a place that's supposed to be safe,

00:04:57.650 --> 00:04:58.900
like a high school dance.

00:05:00.150 --> 00:05:02.520
- I don't feel protected
as a queer person,

00:05:02.520 --> 00:05:04.420
especially as a queer person of color.

00:05:04.470 --> 00:05:06.573
I think at my school specifically,

00:05:06.870 --> 00:05:10.393
for the number of out queer
and trans people that we have,

00:05:10.470 --> 00:05:12.030
there's very little protection

00:05:12.030 --> 00:05:13.683
in terms of enumerated policy.

00:05:14.140 --> 00:05:15.630
I've arguably done more work

00:05:15.630 --> 00:05:17.467
for LGBT inclusivity at my school

00:05:17.467 --> 00:05:19.510
than some of the people who make

00:05:19.510 --> 00:05:20.890
the policies at my school, who,

00:05:20.890 --> 00:05:22.790
it's their literal job to do this work,

00:05:22.790 --> 00:05:24.913
and, so it's been frustrating.

00:05:27.870 --> 00:05:29.803
Ohio is, it's quaint.

00:05:30.240 --> 00:05:31.310
It's one of those places where

00:05:31.310 --> 00:05:33.183
everyone thinks it's just corn.

00:05:33.580 --> 00:05:36.363
There's also a lot of
racism and homophobia,

00:05:36.410 --> 00:05:37.563
in addition to corn.

00:05:37.890 --> 00:05:41.773
When I came out, I didn't have
an official, guys, I'm queer.

00:05:41.780 --> 00:05:44.750
I just started dating a
girl, and everyone was like,

00:05:44.750 --> 00:05:46.918
oh, I didn't know you were gay,
and I'm like, well I'm not.

00:05:46.918 --> 00:05:47.751
And they're like, what are you?

00:05:47.751 --> 00:05:49.060
And I'm like, haven't figured it out yet.

00:05:49.060 --> 00:05:52.803
I think, in terms of coming
out as gender-nonbinary,

00:05:52.930 --> 00:05:54.960
that was a little bit more difficult.

00:05:54.960 --> 00:05:57.150
I got more of, well I
don't know what that means,

00:05:57.150 --> 00:05:58.450
well can you explain that to me,

00:05:58.450 --> 00:06:00.980
well, are you sure that
there's more than two genders,

00:06:00.980 --> 00:06:03.350
and I think people get
caught up on the pronouns,

00:06:03.350 --> 00:06:04.880
like, oh, the different pronouns,

00:06:04.880 --> 00:06:06.853
it's not grammatically correct.

00:06:07.440 --> 00:06:10.470
In reality, they're not
seeing a person saying like,

00:06:10.470 --> 00:06:12.990
hey, I'm different than
what you think I am,

00:06:12.990 --> 00:06:14.010
I need you to accept that.

00:06:14.010 --> 00:06:16.550
Mom, how do you feel about me

00:06:16.550 --> 00:06:18.573
going to Buzzfeed's Queer Prom?

00:06:19.750 --> 00:06:21.820
- I'm happy for you,
I'm glad you got picked,

00:06:21.820 --> 00:06:24.620
'cause I know that was something
that you really wanted.

00:06:24.790 --> 00:06:25.910
I've learned a lot,

00:06:25.910 --> 00:06:30.910
and I'll say it's really made
me think about my life and,

00:06:36.860 --> 00:06:37.853
here it comes.

00:06:42.920 --> 00:06:44.833
High school was really difficult.

00:06:46.080 --> 00:06:47.410
I thought that I had it rough

00:06:47.410 --> 00:06:49.353
because I was the nerd at school.

00:06:49.700 --> 00:06:51.663
I was mistreated by people but,

00:06:54.581 --> 00:06:59.550
they really did all
say wrong, really wrong

00:07:02.210 --> 00:07:06.760
and, I'm sorry, I'm sorry that
you had to go through that.

00:07:06.760 --> 00:07:09.113
- For reference, school was hard because,

00:07:09.440 --> 00:07:10.507
we'd have teachers that are like,

00:07:10.507 --> 00:07:13.630
we're trying to find a
different class for Ose to be in

00:07:13.630 --> 00:07:16.090
because, you know, they make
the teacher uncomfortable,

00:07:16.090 --> 00:07:19.040
or, we understand that this
teacher makes you uncomfortable

00:07:19.040 --> 00:07:20.740
because they don't represent your identity

00:07:20.740 --> 00:07:23.673
but we're not gonna do anything about it.

00:07:23.750 --> 00:07:26.170
And, they'd been like, oh,
we're gonna suspend you,

00:07:26.170 --> 00:07:28.100
like, oh, we're gonna
put you in detention,

00:07:28.100 --> 00:07:29.900
or we're gonna switch your schedule,

00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:32.440
and never getting to
the route of the problem

00:07:32.440 --> 00:07:35.793
and, so yeah, I really appreciate my mom.

00:07:37.000 --> 00:07:37.833
Yeah.

00:07:37.840 --> 00:07:39.696
- And you can be yourself and turn up.

00:07:39.696 --> 00:07:40.529
(laughing)

00:07:40.529 --> 00:07:41.362
- I can turn up?

00:07:41.362 --> 00:07:42.195
- Yeah.

00:07:42.195 --> 00:07:44.220
- Okay, I'll do that, I'll
turn up, I will turn up.

00:07:44.220 --> 00:07:45.053
- Okay.

00:07:45.053 --> 00:07:46.070
- So there's only, like,

00:07:46.070 --> 00:07:48.893
three days left until I go to New York.

00:07:49.287 --> 00:07:51.520
I've never flown and now here I am

00:07:51.530 --> 00:07:53.763
graduating and flying out to New York.

00:07:54.440 --> 00:07:56.193
What a way to start adulthood.

00:07:57.760 --> 00:07:58.860
Hi, my name's Paige,

00:07:58.860 --> 00:08:01.683
I'm 18 years old and I come
from Las Vegas, Nevada.

00:08:01.870 --> 00:08:03.900
I came out to my aunt,
she's my support system.

00:08:03.900 --> 00:08:05.000
I told her everything.

00:08:05.080 --> 00:08:07.930
That's where I would go to
escape from my situation at home.

00:08:07.930 --> 00:08:10.513
She's like that backbone
that I needed growing up.

00:08:10.810 --> 00:08:14.090
So I questioned my grandmother
and my aunt, actually.

00:08:14.090 --> 00:08:15.590
Those are the first two
people I questioned.

00:08:15.590 --> 00:08:17.783
I was like, what is a lesbian?

00:08:18.380 --> 00:08:19.980
'Cause I was like, what is that?

00:08:20.120 --> 00:08:21.940
'Cause that's what I was told that I was,

00:08:21.940 --> 00:08:25.163
and I was like, yeah I like
girls, there's a term for it?

00:08:25.280 --> 00:08:26.500
So when I came out that weekend

00:08:26.500 --> 00:08:28.320
after sitting there and contemplating,

00:08:28.320 --> 00:08:30.573
a 12-year-old sitting
on the couch just like,

00:08:31.130 --> 00:08:34.340
okay, I went up back upstairs and I said,

00:08:34.340 --> 00:08:37.393
you know what, you're right, I am.

00:08:38.322 --> 00:08:39.940
Hey, hey, hey, hey, hey,
hey, hey, hey, hey Sidney.

00:08:39.940 --> 00:08:41.298
- Oh, you caught me in deep thought.

00:08:41.298 --> 00:08:42.950
(laughing)

00:08:42.950 --> 00:08:45.230
- I went to elementary
school, middle school,

00:08:45.230 --> 00:08:46.260
and high school with the same kids,

00:08:46.260 --> 00:08:48.460
so everyone just grew
up knowing each other.

00:08:48.940 --> 00:08:52.733
We don't have a LGBT club.

00:08:52.920 --> 00:08:54.943
We did and they got rid of it.

00:08:55.620 --> 00:08:57.650
When they got rid of it,
I was kinda disappointed.

00:08:57.650 --> 00:09:00.193
I was like, you're serious, right?

00:09:00.740 --> 00:09:01.890
You can't do that.

00:09:01.890 --> 00:09:04.833
You're basically telling us
we can't express ourselves,

00:09:05.270 --> 00:09:08.400
so I grew up my junior year
and senior year without one,

00:09:08.400 --> 00:09:11.020
and you just saw this
decline of people who

00:09:11.410 --> 00:09:13.680
didn't wanna be as open about it at school

00:09:13.680 --> 00:09:16.280
and we just didn't have the club anymore.

00:09:16.770 --> 00:09:18.100
- I was born in Boston.

00:09:18.100 --> 00:09:20.570
I lived there for my first
two years of my life,

00:09:20.570 --> 00:09:22.523
and then I moved to Barbados.

00:09:22.913 --> 00:09:24.920
(calming music)

00:09:24.920 --> 00:09:27.420
Part of growing up there
was, in the culture,

00:09:27.420 --> 00:09:30.980
it's not okay to be who I was,

00:09:30.980 --> 00:09:34.223
so it was a very, very
private part of my life.

00:09:34.820 --> 00:09:36.793
I moved back when I was 10 years old.

00:09:36.850 --> 00:09:40.773
My school was an all boys,
New England Prep School,

00:09:40.890 --> 00:09:43.963
so take with that what you will.

00:09:44.210 --> 00:09:46.610
It's predominately white,
predominately straight,

00:09:46.610 --> 00:09:48.280
so there wasn't much of a community

00:09:48.280 --> 00:09:49.950
for two aspects of my identity.

00:09:49.950 --> 00:09:54.470
So it became difficult to
really exist in that space,

00:09:54.470 --> 00:09:57.370
so that's when I turned to
theater after my freshman year.

00:09:57.370 --> 00:09:59.900
It's something that I
ended up really enjoying

00:09:59.900 --> 00:10:01.903
and it became a huge part of my life.

00:10:02.045 --> 00:10:04.128
- Well, I have some news.

00:10:05.187 --> 00:10:06.020
- Yeah?

00:10:06.230 --> 00:10:07.840
- Well we're super excited that

00:10:07.840 --> 00:10:09.510
you're gonna come hang with us.

00:10:10.202 --> 00:10:13.019
And I love your story.
- Oh my God.

00:10:13.019 --> 00:10:14.210
- We're so stoked.

00:10:14.210 --> 00:10:16.530
- So you're good to go, like you can come,

00:10:16.530 --> 00:10:19.373
you're free, and you're
gonna bring your mom, right?

00:10:19.580 --> 00:10:20.413
- Yeah.

00:10:20.413 --> 00:10:21.530
Oh my God.
- Then she can come?

00:10:21.530 --> 00:10:23.680
- I wish I had told my mom first,

00:10:23.680 --> 00:10:26.580
because that's the only opinion
that I really cared about.

00:10:26.580 --> 00:10:29.253
I remember the story
very, very distinctly.

00:10:29.290 --> 00:10:34.290
December 6, 2017, we're talking
about one of my friends,

00:10:34.580 --> 00:10:38.083
who was going through a really
difficult time in her life,

00:10:38.290 --> 00:10:41.140
and I was asking my mom for advice

00:10:41.140 --> 00:10:43.933
on how I could help her and
help her through this time,

00:10:43.950 --> 00:10:45.210
and she was talking about how,

00:10:45.210 --> 00:10:48.630
oh I just wish kids would
feel more comfortable

00:10:48.630 --> 00:10:49.990
telling their parents
things, so I was like,

00:10:49.990 --> 00:10:52.170
oh, this might be a sign,
lemme just do it right now,

00:10:52.170 --> 00:10:54.240
and it was the longest pause ever

00:10:54.240 --> 00:10:57.080
and it finally set in and she
laughed and was like, I know.

00:10:57.080 --> 00:10:57.913
- I knew.

00:10:58.930 --> 00:11:00.793
I just knew.

00:11:01.040 --> 00:11:05.480
I am happy that he's able
to come out his comfort zone

00:11:05.677 --> 00:11:10.677
and say who he really is, not
being ashamed, and being free.

00:11:17.570 --> 00:11:19.583
I respect that a lot about him.

00:11:22.221 --> 00:11:24.000
(laughing)

00:11:24.000 --> 00:11:26.410
- Yeah, I went to prom,
I went to prom twice,

00:11:26.410 --> 00:11:29.070
and I was with a singular
person that I liked

00:11:29.070 --> 00:11:31.445
in a space full of people
that made me uncomfortable.

00:11:31.445 --> 00:11:33.590
- Like if I wanted to
bring a boy or something,

00:11:33.590 --> 00:11:35.960
I don't think that there would
be space for me to do that.

00:11:35.960 --> 00:11:38.083
- Do I go, do I get judged?

00:11:39.130 --> 00:11:41.523
I don't want that
judgment on my shoulders.

00:11:42.330 --> 00:11:43.163
- It was ugly.

00:11:46.030 --> 00:11:47.513
I lived, I survived that day.

00:11:49.230 --> 00:11:50.063
I made it.

00:11:50.208 --> 00:11:51.200
(laughing)

00:11:51.200 --> 00:11:53.657
I have a good prom coming!

00:11:54.349 --> 00:11:56.182
- [Unison] Queer Prom!

00:11:57.329 --> 00:11:58.454
- I'm excited to meet them.

00:11:58.454 --> 00:12:01.318
- [Jazzmyne] I'm like,
so excited to meet them.

00:12:01.318 --> 00:12:02.151
- Okay.

00:12:05.868 --> 00:12:07.701
- Welcome to New York!

00:12:07.801 --> 00:12:10.051
(cheering)

00:12:11.919 --> 00:12:12.752
What's up?

00:12:13.300 --> 00:12:16.203
- I'm here at Buzzfeed, like, holy crap.

00:12:16.360 --> 00:12:17.513
This is amazing!

00:12:17.750 --> 00:12:18.583
- Surprise.

00:12:18.822 --> 00:12:20.530
(laughing)

00:12:20.530 --> 00:12:21.950
- This is just an adrenaline rush.

00:12:21.950 --> 00:12:23.003
It's like, whoa.

00:12:24.040 --> 00:12:26.433
- We have a little surprise for you.

00:12:27.120 --> 00:12:31.780
We got some new little
phones for you guys.

00:12:31.780 --> 00:12:33.030
- [Curly] So these phones will be

00:12:33.030 --> 00:12:35.503
so y'all can document the Queer Prom,

00:12:36.241 --> 00:12:39.423
and then also y'all can
take them home afterwards.

00:12:39.812 --> 00:12:42.062
(cheering)

00:12:42.880 --> 00:12:44.500
- I don't think anyone understands

00:12:44.500 --> 00:12:46.460
how excited I am to be here.

00:12:46.460 --> 00:12:49.240
- I think probably I'm most
excited about is the energy.

00:12:49.240 --> 00:12:51.850
I never feel like I can just
go and socialize somewhere,

00:12:51.850 --> 00:12:52.910
and I feel like it's gonna be a place

00:12:52.910 --> 00:12:54.550
where I can just talk to
anybody and them be like,

00:12:54.550 --> 00:12:55.383
hey, what's up?

00:12:55.400 --> 00:12:57.470
- I think this is the first
time that I would probably

00:12:57.470 --> 00:13:00.313
be in a room with that
many people who are queer.

00:13:00.480 --> 00:13:01.313
- Exciting.

00:13:01.830 --> 00:13:04.590
- I am so excited to
just click with everybody

00:13:04.590 --> 00:13:07.490
and run around and touch everything.

00:13:07.490 --> 00:13:09.040
If it's shiny, I'm touching it.

00:13:09.080 --> 00:13:11.240
- Alright, everybody, make a silly face!

00:13:11.240 --> 00:13:12.530
Three, two, one.

00:13:12.530 --> 00:13:13.630
- [Unison] Queer Prom!

00:13:16.213 --> 00:13:18.713
(funky music)

